course: dictionary
lesson: 5859
title: Mammoth: an animal and an adjective
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have two jobs. Mammoth can be a noun, a name for an animal, or an adjective that describes something as very big. Read the words around it to find which job it is doing. «The mammoth roamed the snowy plains» names an animal, but «It was a mammoth task» tells you the task was huge.
explain: The animal was real. Woolly mammoths were hairy relatives of elephants, and they lived during the last Ice Age, long after the dinosaurs. Scientists know about them from bones, teeth and tusks dug up in many countries, including Britain and the United States. «The last woolly mammoths died out about 4,000 years ago.»
explain: When you meet a new word, ask what would fit in its place. If you put «huge» into «a mammoth queue» and it still makes sense, mammoth means very big there. Then check your meaning by reading the whole sentence again.
fact: A mammoth was a huge, hairy animal like an elephant, with long curved tusks.
fact: Mammoths lived long ago and have died out, so none are alive today.
fact: As an adjective, «mammoth» means very, very big, as in «a mammoth meal».
fact: Mammoth bones and teeth are dug up in many countries, because mammoths roamed widely across the northern half of the world.
fact: Carbon dating works only for things up to about 50,000 years old, such as mammoths and old bones; dinosaurs are too old for it.
exercise: What was a mammoth? | A tiny insect with six legs | A small bird that sings at dawn | *A huge, hairy animal like an elephant that lived long ago | A fast kind of train
exercise: «It was a mammoth job to clean the whole school.» What does mammoth mean here? | Very cheap | *Very, very big | Very quiet | Very wet
exercise: «Woolly mammoths, hairy relatives of elephants, lived during the last Ice Age.» Mammoths were relatives of which animal? | Cats | *Elephants | Dinosaurs | Sloths
test: «The cartoon mammoth travels with a sabre-toothed cat, but the cartoon sloth is smaller than the real one.» In the cartoon «Ice Age», were the animals real? | Only the mammoth was real, and it could talk | No, they were all made up by the cartoonists | Only the cat was real | *Yes, all three were real animals, though they never talked
test: «Carbon dating works only for things up to about 50,000 years old, such as mammoths.» Why is carbon dating useful for mammoths? | It shows how mammoths sang | *Mammoth bones are young enough for it to work | Carbon dating only works on dinosaurs | Mammoths are too old for it
exam: Which sentence uses mammoth as an adjective meaning very big? | Mammoths died out about 4,000 years ago | Its tusks were long and curved | The mammoth lived in the Arctic | *The mammoth pile of washing took all afternoon to fold
